  "summary_en": "Swiss DETEC ordinance (version of 1 August 2024) regulating special-category aircraft, including hang gliders, kites, balloons, parachutes, model aircraft and other unmanned aircraft. It supplements EU drone rules, sets operating bans, minimum pilot ages, liability insurance, U-Space provisions, and qualified-entity accreditation.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "EU drone regulations 2019/945 and 2019/947 apply primarily to unmanned aircraft, with the ordinance supplementing them.",
   "Drone operation is banned near airfields, over prisons, military areas, power substations and nuclear plants, with exceptions by permit.",
   "Minimum remote pilot ages of 12 (open category) and 14, and 5 for unsupervised model flying.",
   "Liability insurance of at least CHF 1 million is required for aircraft over 250 g.",
   "BAZL may accredit qualified entities and designate U-Space airspaces with service-provider obligations."
  ],
